# Direct dependencies — the only file to hand-edit.
#
# requirements.txt is COMPILED from this and pins every transitive dependency
# too. Streamlit Community Cloud installs from requirements.txt, so the lock has
# to live there to reach production; editing it by hand loses the lock.
#
# Regenerate after any change here (see the header of requirements.txt):
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --universal --python-version 3.12 \
#       --output-file requirements.txt
#
# Then verify on BOTH interpreters — dev runs 3.12, Cloud runs 3.13, and a pin
# that resolves is not the same as a pin that installs (tasks/lessons.md,
# 2026-08-07):
#   uv venv /tmp/v312 --python 3.12
#   VIRTUAL_ENV=/tmp/v312 uv pip install -r requirements.txt pytest pytest-mock pytest-timeout
#   /tmp/v312/bin/python -m pytest tests/
#   (repeat with --python 3.13)

